diff --git a/guidance.md b/guidance.md
index a6994b1..51fc2ea 100644
--- a/guidance.md
+++ b/guidance.md
@@ -1 +1,9 @@
 Use the provided spreadsheet tools to complete the requested workbook. Preserve source inputs.
+
+Working method:
+- Inspect the source workbook first, and read every comment: comments state the intended business rule, the required units, and the base-to-scenario distinction.
+- Enter Excel formulas (strings beginning with "=") in the target cells rather than hard-coded numbers. Anchor one formula per row and let relative references fill every displayed period.
+- Cover every column that has a period header. A row counts as complete only when every displayed period is filled, including the first forecast column. A value in a period column to the left of the first forecast column, or a section labelled historical, is a base for the projection, not a substitute for the first forecast period.
+- Keep each figure in the unit the row header states. When an input unit differs from the display unit the comment requires, convert inside the formula.
+- Do not fill cells the source marks or leaves intentionally blank, and keep the original labels, units and note text untouched.
+- After writing, run workbook_verify and confirm every formula resolves to a plausible value with no formula errors before delivering.
